| A USB 2.0 full-speed host's receiving port, as seen from a device's
| receptacle: a stand-in (synthetic, linear tables) built from the USB 2.0
| specification's limits, not from any vendor's file. The host itself is
| off-board and unknown, so its own model is the spec's envelope.
|
|   C_comp      CIN, transceiver input capacitance: <= 20 pF (USB 2.0
|               table 7-7). typ 10 pF, min 5 pF, max 20 pF.
|   Vinl/Vinh   the single-ended receiver thresholds, 0.8 V / 2.0 V.
|   [Diff Pin]  the differential receiver's sensitivity, 200 mV (VDI).
|   [GND Clamp] the host's 15 kohm D+/D- pull-down (RPD, 14.25..24.8 k),
|               linear: min = 24.8 k, max = 14.25 k.
|
| The cable between the receptacle and the host is not modelled: what this
| file sits behind is the board's own trace, which is what a board's
| routing rules are about.
